      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lewisburg%2C_Ohio",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The village was named for Lewisburg, Virginia, which is now part of West Virginia.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lewisburg%2C_Ohio",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Pioneer John Mumma founded the nearby community of Euphemia in 1836, and it merged with Lewisburg in 1916.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1,
        9,
        12
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
